<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 30,427 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 30,427 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 30,427 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 38,416 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 9,990	    12,630</p>
<p>    Import cargo			20,437	    25,786</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours, seven ships were expected to sail and 10 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Chemicals		 7,350	 Bakri Orbitor	 6/8</p>
<p>Crude oil		67,658	 Johar		   6/8</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 42,000	 Trade Resolve	 4/8</p>
<p>Sugar		    13,000	 Nan Jiang	     5/8</p>
<p>Vegoil		   18,600	 Kiristal		due</p>
<p>High speed diesel    70,000	 Chesapeak City	due</p>
<p>Sugar		    14,000	 Won San		 due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
